Accepted by the main session, 2026-08-10.

NewFetcher and FetchAt measure 0% in the unit-coverage run because their
only honest exercise needs a real broker: FetchAt's contract (direct
assignment at the pointer offset, poll, verified classification) is
exactly what the roadmap's verification criterion tests via the
integration suite, which is build-tagged (-tags integration) and
therefore invisible to the unit coverage run.

That suite is step 2 of the frozen plan rpkv-02-fetch
(fetch/fetcher_integration_test.go, roadmap criteria (a)(b)(c)) and lands
on this same branch before anything is pushed. Unit-mocking *kgo.Client
would test the mock, not the contract, and contradict the black-box
contract-test discipline (repo CLAUDE.md, ADR-002).

verifyFetch - the classification logic that can be unit-tested - is at
100%.
